# Everything that shows the project's history IS committed, so every PC sees the same state after a pull:
# the book (LiberPrimus.pdf), the 75 original page images (work/orig/), the PDF page renders (work/pages/),
# figures, all results and logs (results/, including each machine's runner logs in results/overnight/<machine>/),
# scratch outputs and review sheets (work/tmp/), engine run outputs (work/phpmt/data/, work/walk/data/),
# the write-ups (work/log/, docs/) and all code.
#
# Only what each machine builds for itself is ignored. After a pull, `python jobs/overnight.py run selftest`
# (or jobs/setup.sh) rebuilds it on that machine.

# --- built on each machine: compiled engines and the generated keystream library (13 MB, ~4 min to build) ---
work/phpmt/target/
work/phpmt/target_gen/
work/walk/target/
work/kscreen/target/
work/kscreen/data/
work/layer2/target/
work/layer2/data/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/

# --- this PC's runner alias (see jobs/overnight.py); never the real computer name ---
.lp_machine

# --- transient files of a running job ---
results/overnight/*/runner*.lock
*.part
results/overnight/*/*.tmp
*.failed

# --- third-party documents read during research: not ours to redistribute (see work/log/research_2026-10-16.md) ---
work/ref/wulfic/
work/ref/outguessed/

work/ref/deepseek/

work/tmp/advsep_bitcheck/kscreen_old.exe

work/h5rs/target/

# --- chanscreen (GPT, 2026-10-19): per-case raw records (about 300 KB each, hundreds of cases) and local builds stay out of git; the frozen protocol, code, tests,
#     summaries, thresholds, hashes and logs are tracked. The raw records are reproducible from the frozen seeds; a SHA-256 manifest of them is committed instead. ---
work/chanscreen/raw/
work/chanscreen/build/

# --- ogscan (own OutGuess-style reader, 2026-10-19): per-page bit lists (about 0.8 MB each) and the Rust build are reproducible and stay out of git ---
work/ogscan/bits/
work/ogscan/target/

# third-party archive (data, never committed)
Other repositories and work/
work/ref/discord_464/
